    "notes": "Q61370117 and OSM way 667587311 identify the bridge. Current PMTiles S62 lines identify the twin southwest tunnel mouths, full carriageways and staggered northeast joins. Pylon stations follow visible aerial base and shadow traces. Pylon leg profiles, stay counts and roadway fittings are photo-based approximations. The exterior model includes both tunnel mouths and 20 m of recessed lining capped in shadow. The native S62 tunnel paths continue below terrain. A local opening fits only the portal mouths to the coarse hill. The current map gives the carriageway endpoints and a 2,124.51 m axis envelope. The retained 1,116.03 m bridge polygon is partial. The 2,135 m reference length is recorded separately. Physical-device timings are unmeasured."
  },
